      "filename": "Grand Canyon National Park, Ranger Guided Hike To Cedar Ridge - 0251 - Flickr - Grand Canyon NPS.jpg",
      "title": "File:Grand Canyon National Park, Ranger Guided Hike To Cedar Ridge - 0251 - Flickr - Grand Canyon NPS.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b9/Grand_Canyon_National_Park%2C_Ranger_Guided_Hike_To_Cedar_Ridge_-_0251_-_Flickr_-_Grand_Canyon_NPS.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grand_Canyon_National_Park,_Ranger_Guided_Hike_To_Cedar_Ridge_-_0251_-_Flickr_-_Grand_Canyon_NPS.jpg",
      "width": 8000,
      "height": 2742,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "Grand Canyon National Park",
      "description": "Step into the panorama on a ranger guided hike to Cedar Ridge on the South Kaibab Trail. Offered daily during the summer. The hike departs early each morning on the South Rim. Check at the Visitor Center for the exact time.\nDiscover the canyon's beauty while descending 1,120 feet (340 m) on an unpaved trail. This strenuous 3-mile (5 km), round-trip hike is not recommended for people with heart or respiratory problems or difficulty walking. Bring 1–2 quarts (liters) of water, sunscreen, hat, snacks, and sturdy hiking shoes. Allow 3-4 hours to do the hike. \n\nNPS photo by M. Quinn, May 12, 2013.",
      "dateCreated": "2013-05-12 09:51",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "south-kaibab-trail-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "9w2m",
      "mediumPath": "_m/9/w/2/m/south-kaibab-trail-wp/grand-canyon-national-park-ran-medium.webp",
      "smallPath": "_m/9/w/2/m/south-kaibab-trail-wp/grand-canyon-national-park-ran-small.webp"
    },
